Summary:
During today’s session, the focus was on revising core MongoDB concepts to strengthen understanding of database management. Key topics such as collections, documents, CRUD operations, and basic schema design were reviewed. Attention was given to how MongoDB integrates with backend applications and handles data storage. This revision helped in reinforcing the fundamental concepts required for working with databases.

Outcomes:
By the end of the session, there was a clearer understanding of how MongoDB manages data and supports application development. The revision improved confidence in performing basic database operations and structuring data effectively. It also enhanced knowledge of integrating MongoDB with backend systems. Overall, the session strengthened foundational skills in working with MongoDB.
